/-!
# The coset setup and initial reductions in 15.3.48–49

The development defines the relative quotient actions, the normal core in
F.9.1(a), and its two-residual. It proves 15.3.49(1) from 15.3.7's actual
product factorization and derives F.9.1(c), (d), and (e) from the earlier
local conclusions.

The commutator-duality argument is complete: after the faithful-action and
omega-bound calculations, it derives the central containment of U_H and
elementary abelianness of both U_H and V_H. Their spans are kept distinct.

The complete verification of F.9.1, generalized-Fitting centralization and
faithfulness, the extraspecial omega bound, and the remaining prime-support
reductions are still outstanding. Thus this module does not yet assert all
of 15.3.48 or the full initial reduction of 15.3.49.

Source: Aschbacher–Smith, combined manuscript (1 March 2004), pp.1141–1143.
-/
